compiler/test — the compiler's suites
=====================================

Where a new case goes
---------------------
  test/test_*.c             plain C, exit code is the verdict. Assertions come
                            from ../../testkit/javelina_test.h (CHECK,
                            CHECK_CASE, CHECK_EXPR, TEST_FAILED, TEST_SUMMARY).
                            A suite that evaluates zero checks FAILS — silence
                            from a test that never asserted is indistinguishable
                            from success.

  test/test_exec.c          compiler output EXECUTED in the VM. The fast pin for
                            a behaviour: compile a program, run it, assert the
                            result. Reaches the VM only through the public
                            wasm.h (via test/exec.h) — no jav_* internals.

  conformance/              e2e breadth: real .java programs with expected
                            stdout and exit code, driven through the SHIPPED
                            javelinac + javelina binaries, both tiers — see
                            conformance/README.md. Runs as the last leg of
                            `make test` (`make test-java-conformance`).

  test/test_cli.sh          the shipped binaries end to end — argv, exit codes,
                            stderr diagnostics, -jit vs -nojit agreement. Runs
                            in the default gate (`make test` at the root).

The rule that matters
---------------------
A bug that only the e2e corpus catches is a failure of the FAST suites, not just
of the code. Pin it at the level that owns it — test_sir for a lowering,
test_click_partition for a lattice/partition fact, test_exec for a behaviour —
and verify the pin RED against a deliberate break before trusting it. The e2e
layer confirms breadth; it must never be what DISCOVERS a defect.

Never put our own material in ../../testsuite/. That is a git submodule pinned
to the upstream WebAssembly corpus: files of ours there are outside javelina's
history and are destroyed by any submodule operation. Four VM fixture sources
were lost exactly that way.

Running one suite
-----------------
    make test-one T=test_sema      # from compiler/
    make test-one T=test_sema      # from the repo root — routes by name
    make test-sema                 # the historical dashed name still works

A failing suite prints its whole log; logs are kept in ../build/logs/.
`make test-exec-asan` builds and runs the execution corpus under AddressSanitizer.
